Telegram Video Streamer Deployment Guide
Prerequisites:
Hostinger VPS (Ubuntu 20.04/22.04)
A domain name configured to point to your VPS IP
SSH access to the server
Deployment Steps
1. Upload Project Files
Unzip the project to /opt/tg_streamer:

bash
sudo mkdir -p /opt/tg_streamer
sudo chown $(whoami):$(whoami) /opt/tg_streamer
unzip tg_streamer.zip -d /opt/tg_streamer
2. Create an Environment File
Create a .env file inside /opt/tg_streamer:

INI
BOT_TOKEN=YOUR_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
3. Install Python Dependencies
bash
cd /opt/tg_streamer
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
4. Configure Nginx
Set up Nginx for the streamer:

bash
sudo cp nginx/tg-streamer.conf /etc/nginx/sites-available/tg_streamer
sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/tg_streamer /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl restart nginx
5. Setup Systemd Service
Create a system service for the app:

bash
sudo cp systemd/tg-streamer.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl start tg-streamer
sudo systemctl enable tg-streamer
6. Configure Firewall and SSL
Enable firewall rules and set up SSL certificates:

bash
sudo ufw allow 80
sudo apt install certbot python3-certbot-nginx -y
sudo certbot --nginx -d yourdomain.com
7. Usage
Upload a video to the Telegram bot and retrieve the file_id from the bot's response.
Access the video player using the URL:
https://yourdomain.com/player?file_id=<file_id>
Enjoy seamless video streaming through your Telegram bot!
